    "m2_prompt_trader_proposal_original": "**Action**: Hold\n\n**Reasoning**: The investment plan's Hold recommendation is well-supported by the evidence. The technical picture is clearly bearish \u2014 price ($163.22) sits below all major moving averages (10 EMA $167.36, 20 SMA, 50 SMA $173.24 declining, 200 SMA), the MACD just crossed bearish on 4/19, and RSI at 37.90 is not yet oversold with no reversal signal. However, the fundamentals are genuinely strong with $39.9B quarterly operating cash flow and a fortress balance sheet, and the bear himself concedes this is not a sell. With technicals and fundamentals diverging sharply and neither side holding a decisive edge, the disciplined stance is to hold current position and wait for confirmation \u2014 either a technical reversal (RSI below 30 turning up, bullish MACD crossover, price reclaiming the 10 EMA) or a fundamental catalyst (next earnings confirming cash flow strength). The risk-reward is roughly 1.2:1 to 1.4:1, barely better than a coin flip, so initiating new longs is speculative while selling ignores the strong balance sheet.\n\n**Entry Price**: 163.22\n\n**Stop Loss**: 162.31\n\n**Position Sizing**: Maintain current position at current weight; do not add or trim. If adding on confirmation signals, scale in gradually in 25-33% increments.\n\nFINAL TRANSACTION PROPOSAL: **HOLD**",
